  "narrative": "The new analyses substantially strengthen the dataset-specific association map and mostly reject the proposed masking interactions. TP53 loss remains associated with weaker dependency inside KEAP1-loss cells, H50 signed +0.576, interval +0.414 to +0.739, so I accept and close that context claim. KEAP1 loss remains associated with weaker dependency among TP53-intact cells, H54 signed +0.780, interval +0.719 to +0.841, also accepted. SMARCA4 loss remains associated with much stronger dependency among TP53-intact cells, H55 signed +0.833, interval +0.779 to +0.887, accepted. TP53 loss also remains associated with weaker dependency among SMARCA4-loss cells, H56 signed +0.412, interval +0.206 to +0.618, accepted. These results indicate that the dominant SMARCA4, KEAP1, and TP53 associations are not explained by simple mutual dilution; they persist across each other's co-mutation contexts. They remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal mechanisms.  PTEN results are now more coherent but remain post-hoc and multiplicity-sensitive. The two-restricted low-mask PTEN claim H58, among TP53-intact and KEAP1-intact cells, gives signed +0.255, interval +0.165 to +0.345, and is accepted. More unexpectedly, PTEN loss is also associated with stronger dependency within KEAP1-loss cells, H51 signed +0.378, interval +0.193 to +0.562, accepted despite the smaller KEAP1-loss sample. This argues against a simple masking interpretation in KEAP1-loss cells. The PTEN-by-TP53 interaction H62 is not compelling: point estimate +0.157 but interval -0.145 to +0.459, including zero and much smaller values, so I reject it. The PTEN-by-KEAP1 interaction H63 is in the opposite claimed direction and rejected. The PTEN-by-SMARCA4 interaction H64 and the broad PTEN effect within TP53-loss cells H59 are also not threshold-exceeding; H59 point estimate is +0.102 and interval includes zero, so I reject those claims. The SMARCA4-by-TP53 interaction H65 is near null, supporting additive independence of the SMARCA4-loss and TP53-loss associations, and is rejected. Because H50 directly supports a large TP53-loss context effect within KEAP1-loss cells, I also reassess H38, the earlier TP53-by-KEAP1 interaction, and reject it as not providing threshold-exceeding evidence for interaction.  PTEN within adenocarcinoma H52 remains borderline: signed +0.207, interval +0.097 to +0.317. The point estimate is meaningful, but the lower bound is below the 0.15-unit threshold, so it cannot be accepted. I defer it rather than close it because the new PTEN-by-TP53 co-occurrence pattern makes adenocarcinoma with TP53 intact a plausible cleaner context; I register that refinement for possible follow-up. For validation, I request H39, the accepted PTEN association among TP53-intact cells. This is the most valuable remaining validation target because the central SMARCA4, KEAP1, and broad TP53 claims have already been validated, whereas PTEN remains the key post-hoc context-dependent finding. Independent confirmation of H39 would strengthen whether PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency in the supplied dataset outside TP53-loss contexts.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 4 appraise state: Accepted dataset-specific associations: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency broadly and in ARID1A-intact, adenocarcinoma, TP53-intact contexts; KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency broadly, in TP53-intact cells, and in co-mutation-restricted cells; TP53 loss -> weaker dependency broadly and in KEAP1-loss and SMARCA4-loss contexts. PTEN loss -> stronger dependency in TP53-intact cells, TP53/KEAP1-intact cells, triple TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact cells, and KEAP1-loss cells, all post-hoc/context-specific. PTEN broad H32 remains unresolved because lower bound is below threshold, but validation H39 has been requested. Rejected masking interactions: PTEN-by-TP53, PTEN-by-KEAP1, PTEN-by-SMARCA4, SMARCA4-by-TP53, PTEN in TP53-loss cells, and TP53-by-KEAP1 interaction after direct context H50. PTEN in adenocarcinoma H52 unresolved/deferred, with registered refinement PTEN in adenocarcinoma and TP53-intact. Remaining broad/low-priority untested claims: H18 research marker F, H25 BRCA2, H26 MSI-high, H43 DNA-omics completeness, H44 KY library, H45 BRAF, H46 EGFR amp, H47 ERBB2 amp, H49 NF1, H53 CDKN2A in TP53 loss, H57 KEAP1 in SMARCA4 loss, H60 SMARCA4 in STK11 loss, H61 KEAP1 in STK11 loss. Next allocation should prioritize validation follow-up, PTEN subtype/context refinement, and remaining broad predictors only if they are cheap or useful for completeness."
}

